DEFLIST(1)                  UNIX Programmer's Manual                  DEFLIST(1)

NAME
     deflist - the hanging tag, and what happens when it does not fit

DESCRIPTION
     -l   A tag that fits the five-column step keeps its body on the tag's line,
          which is the shape v7's .TP has always had.

     -1ACFRacdfgilqrstu
          A tag wider than the step gets the next line to itself, and the body
          starts under it.

     -x   A body may hold more than one paragraph.

          This is the second, and it is indented to the same column as the
          first.

     -n   A body may hold another container, and the step applies again:

          -    a bullet inside a definition
          -    and a second one

          -inner
               a definition inside a definition

          A definition with no term above it keeps its shape and loses nothing.

     -abcd
          A tag exactly as wide as the step, five columns, is too wide for it:
          there has to be a space after the tag, so the body goes on the next
          line.

     -abc One column narrower, and it fits with the one space.
